# MiniMax live probe — test key in bashrc

Native MiniMax work (payload, vision, tools, `reasoning_split`, model cards,
gear panel, trim, canary diagnosis) must live-probe the vendor **before**
claiming ChatHub is wrong or shipping a MiniMax adapter change.

## Credentials — these names are fixed

On this host they are already set in **`~/.bashrc`**:

- `MINIMAX_API_KEY`
- `MINIMAX_PROXY_URL`

Use **those two names**. Do not invent `PROBE_MINIMAX_*`, and do not map MiniMax
onto `PROBE_OPENAICOMPATIBLE_*`. That skill is for generic OpenAI-compatible
gateways (`/v1/responses` + cache matrix), not native MiniMax Chat Completions.

Non-interactive shells often skip `~/.bashrc`. Parse/export those two names from
the file. **Never print `MINIMAX_API_KEY`.** Reporting `key_len` and the proxy
host/path is enough.

## Probe shape

Call `$MINIMAX_PROXY_URL` (Chat Completions `/chat/completions`, `GET /models`)
with `Authorization: Bearer $MINIMAX_API_KEY`. Default model `MiniMax-M3`.
Send the **ChatHub-shaped** body (`buildMinimaxOpenAIChatPayload` + factory
`stream` / `stream_options` / `user`), not only a vendor hello.

Official contract: [Chat Completions](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/api-reference/text-chat-openai),
[M3 tools](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/guides/text-m3-function-call),
[error codes](https://platform.minimaxi.com/docs/api-reference/errorcode.md)
(`2013` = parameter error). Vision `detail` is `low` | `default` | `high`
(not OpenAI `auto`).

Report HTTP status, MiniMax `error.type` / `error.message` / `base_resp`,
latency, usage counts. No prompts, no response text, no secrets.
